config-connector-extensions patch 0058: mockgcp serves a hierarchical
firewall policy's packet mirroring rules: firewallPolicies.addPacketMirroringRule,
getPacketMirroringRule, patchPacketMirroringRule, removePacketMirroringRule.

For compute.gcp.hfl.dev ComputeFirewallPolicyPacketMirroringRule. The
calls are in the compute beta and alpha APIs only, so mockgcp's v1 protos
have no RPC or HTTP route for them; they are served on the HTTP layer,
before the beta-to-v1 rewrite, on the policy the v1 RPCs store, with the
rules of a network firewall policy's packet mirroring rules (patch 0032,
whose helpers this uses): a rule is addressed by its priority, a missing
priority is a 400, a taken priority is refused on add, a patch replaces
the rule, tlsInspect and an INGRESS rule without a source are refused.
Operations are global organization operations, as the firewall policy's
other calls. Upstream candidate: with 0032, once mockgcp has beta protos.

